DASH.todo={title:"What to do as a normal investor",note:"General info, not personal financial advice.",
l:["<b>Don't chase a one-day surge.</b> The S&P jumped 4.7% on Huang's return, but it is still below its 6 Oct record and NYSE new lows (146) still beat new highs (14). Stick to your plan rather than trading on one day's move.",
"<b>Keep investing regularly, not all at once.</b> Fear & Greed is 17, still extreme fear. Fixed monthly buys (DCA) beat guessing whether the bottom is in, which nobody can call.",
"<b>Check your AI and chip exposure.</b> Nvidia fell 14% on Friday and rose 31% on Monday. If one theme has grown into a big share of your money, trim back to your plan; a broad index fund already holds the big AI names.",
"<b>Cash and short bonds earn while you wait.</b> 2-year Treasuries pay ~4.66% and a December Fed hike is ~98% priced. Keep your emergency fund and near-term money there, not in stocks.",
"<b>Plan for higher loan rates.</b> The NY Fed's Williams says there is 'still work to do' on inflation and markets expect a hike on 9 Dec. Lock fixed rates where you can and avoid new variable-rate debt.",
"<b>Gold is a hedge, not a rescue.</b> It jumped 3.9% on Monday to ~$3,649, but that was still its second-lowest settle this year. Keep only a small slice for protection.",
"<b>Keep crypto small.</b> Bitcoin (~$61,200) lagged the stock rally and faded during US hours; only invest what you can afford to see fall a lot more.",
"<b>Thai investors: stay defensive.</b> The SET barely moved (1,454.49) while Wall Street surged; foreigners bought ฿682M on Monday but are still about −฿5.5B for November. Favour steady dividend payers and avoid using margin.",
"<b>Fuel is getting cheaper, for now.</b> US diesel is ~$5.82 (AAA), down from ~$6.00 a week ago, and Brent hit a 3-month low, but tankers keep getting hit near Hormuz. Budget for swings."]};
// Glossary: m = regex matched against an element's text (li/td/h2); d = plain explanation + what it means now.
DASH.glossary={
fg:{m:"Fear & Greed",d:"CNN's 0-100 mood gauge for US stocks, built from 7 signals. 17 (16.97) = Extreme Fear, up from 10 at Friday's close after Monday's rally; 31 a week ago and 17 a month ago. Five of the seven signals still read extreme fear; price strength and the VIX read fear."},
fgbands:{d:"0-25 Extreme Fear, 26-45 Fear, 46-55 Neutral, 56-75 Greed, 76-100 Extreme Greed. Fear often comes before rebounds, but not always."},
nk:{m:"Nuclear Escalation",d:"Our editorial 0-100 tension score from weighted news factors. Not a probability. ~52.2 = Elevated (up from 51.7): Iran vows 'all available means' against the US blockade, three more tankers hit mines near Hormuz, and Russian strikes killed at least 15 near Kyiv."},
nkbands:{d:"0-20 Low, 21-40 Guarded, 41-60 Elevated, 61-80 High, 81-100 Severe. Each factor's score × weight adds up to the total."},
mom:{m:"Market momentum",d:"S&P 500 vs its 125-day average. 3.2 = extreme fear, up from 0.2 after Monday's 4.7% jump."},
str:{m:"price strength",d:"Stocks at 52-week highs vs lows. 28.4 = fear, up from 27.2; NYSE had 146 new lows vs 14 highs on Monday, far fewer lows than Friday's 565."},
brd:{m:"breadth",d:"Volume in rising vs falling stocks. 17.0 = extreme fear, from 20.0, even after Monday's rally."},
pc:{m:"Put/Call",d:"Compares bets on stocks falling vs rising. 6.6 = extreme fear, up from 2.0: still heavy demand for downside protection."},
vix:{m:"VIX",d:"The market's 'fear gauge' of expected S&P swings. 39.0 on CNN's 0-100 scale = fear (from 1.3), as the VIX fell to ~26.6 from ~35.9."},
sh:{m:"Safe-haven",d:"Stock returns vs bonds lately. 6.4 = extreme fear, up from 0.8 as stocks beat bonds on Monday."},
jb:{m:"Junk bond",d:"Extra yield on risky company debt. 18.2 = extreme fear, up from 16.2."},
f1:{m:"Active wars",d:"Wars that could pull in nuclear powers. Scored 74 (from 73): Iran vows 'all available means' against the US blockade, calling it military aggression; Trump says Iran fired more drones and missiles last week than at any time in the war."},
f2:{m:"Russia-Ukraine",d:"A nuclear power at war. Scored 46 (from 45): Russian strikes killed at least 15 in the Kyiv region and Ukraine says it sank a Russian corvette off Libya, though Zelensky says he is ready for four-party talks."},
f3:{m:"spillover",d:"Risk the Mideast war widens. Scored 92 (unchanged): Iran says three more tankers hit mines in Hormuz, and a Houthi-linked outlet says a Saudi strike on Hodeida killed 17."},
f4:{m:"diplomacy channels",d:"Are big powers talking? Higher = fewer working channels. Scored 10 (unchanged): Qatar's PM met Rubio to revive US-Iran talks and Zelensky offers four-party talks, but nothing is scheduled."},
f5:{m:"Arms-control",d:"Nuclear threats and treaty news. Scored 31 (unchanged): Trump says he wants a 'permanent' deal so Iran can never get a nuclear weapon; no arms-control talks are set."},
sp:{m:"S&P",d:"500 big US companies, the main US stock benchmark. ~7,237 Monday (+4.73%), its best day since April 2025 after Nvidia reinstated Jensen Huang, ending a seven-day losing streak; futures dipped ~0.2% in the evening."},
dow:{m:"Dow",d:"30 large 'blue-chip' US stocks, more old-economy. +3.01% (+1,448 pts) Monday to about 49,595, more than reversing Friday's loss."},
ndq:{m:"Nasdaq",d:"Tech-heavy US index. +6.51% Monday to about 24,090, its best day since April 2025; the Nasdaq 100 rose 6.9%."},
y10:{m:"10Y",d:"Yield on 10-year US government bonds, which drives loan rates. ~4.92% Monday, little changed (+1bp); the 2Y rose ~5bp to ~4.66% as hike bets firmed."},
wti:{m:"WTI",d:"US crude oil price. ~$80.2 at Monday's settle (−3.88%), the lowest since 10 Aug, on rising Middle East flows and a Libyan pipeline restart."},
brent:{m:"Brent",d:"Global benchmark crude. ~$89.4 at Monday's settle (−3.46%), the lowest since 31 Aug."},
dsl:{m:"diesel",d:"US average diesel price. ~$5.82/gal (AAA, 23 Nov), down from ~$6.00 a week ago."},
gold:{m:"^Gold$|Gold and|gold slice",d:"Classic safe haven. ~$3,649 Comex settle Monday (+3.90%), the biggest % gain since February, though still the second-lowest settle this year; spot ~$3,627 early Tuesday."},
btc:{m:"Bitcoin|BTC",d:"The largest crypto. ~$61.2k early Tuesday = still bearish: it briefly topped $64,000 on Monday but faded in US hours, lagging the stock rally; it trades with tech, not as a haven."},
bull:{d:"BULLISH = we expect it to rise or hold strong. MILDLY = a leaning, not a strong view."},
neu:{d:"NEUTRAL = no clear direction; it could go either way."},
bear:{d:"BEARISH = we expect it to fall or stay weak."},
ff:{m:"Fed funds",d:"The Fed's key short-term interest rate. 3.75-4.00% after September's hike, held 28 Oct; a December hike to 4.00-4.25% is ~98% priced for 8-9 Dec."},
cpi:{m:"CPI",d:"Consumer price inflation. October rose 0.4% MoM (est. 0.3%) and core 0.3% (est. 0.2%), a third straight upside surprise; no official YoY because of last year's data gap, well above the Fed's 2% goal."},
ppi:{m:"PPI",d:"Prices businesses pay, an early inflation signal. October rose 0.3% MoM (est. 0.4%) and 6.5% YoY, the highest since November 2022; core +0.3%."},
odds:{m:"Hike odds|Fed odds",d:"Market-implied chance of a Fed hike (fed funds futures, CME FedWatch). ~98% for a quarter point in December as of 23 Nov, up from ~88% Friday; Macquarie says 50bp 'feels like an impossibility'."},
dxy:{m:"Dollar index",d:"DXY: the dollar against 6 major currencies. ~104.3 early Tuesday, the strongest since March 2025."},
jpy:{m:"USD/JPY|Yen",d:"Yen per dollar. ~159.0 early Tuesday; the yen slipped 0.2% Monday and is near the 160 level where Japan has warned about intervention."},
cds:{m:"CDS",d:"Credit default swap: insurance against a company defaulting. CoreWeave's CDS went past 11% (a distress level) in October; its bonds now yield ~15% (CNBC, 17 Nov)."},
bot:{m:"BOT policy|BoT meeting|BOT MPC|BoT decision|BoT held|BoT kept",d:"Bank of Thailand's key rate. Held at 1.00% on 28 Oct; Governor Witai says the BoT aims to keep rates steady to support growth but is data-dependent; 2026 GDP forecast kept at 2.4%; next decision 23 Dec."},
set:{m:"SET",d:"SET = Thai stock index; SET50 = its 50 biggest stocks. 1,454.49 on Mon 23 Nov (+1.21, +0.08%), range 1,444.50-1,458.55; Maybank sees support at 1,435-1,440 and resistance at 1,470-1,475."},
flow:{m:"Foreign flows|foreigners",d:"Net buying minus selling by foreign investors. +฿682M of Thai stocks on Mon 23 Nov; −฿5,473M so far in November; foreign firms net bought ฿2,178M of Thai bonds outright on Monday."},
dca:{m:"DCA",d:"Dollar-cost averaging: invest a fixed amount on a schedule regardless of price, which smooths out bad timing."}};

